  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Carson Whisenhunt bought them just enough, and they cashed it.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't leave games on the table when pitching gives them air. Whisenhunt scattered four hits across 5.2 innings. Not dominant, but durable. And the bullpen did what it had to do. Seymour worked two clean frames with two strikeouts. Brubaker closed it. That structure held. The offense didn't need to dominate. They needed one run to matter more than Houston's one, and in the fourth inning, it did. Cavanaugh drove in the difference. They protected it for five innings after. This is how narrow margins feel when they go your way. Not comfortable, just enough.",
